    "owner_mim_id": "MIM:0000057",
    "owner_primary_identifier": "cas:1040352-40-6",
    "owner_grounding": {
      "ontology_id": "CHEBI:27469",
      "ontology_label": "2-dehydro-D-gluconic acid",
      "ontology_source": "CHEBI",
      "mapping_quality": "NARROW_MATCH",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "evidence_type": "DATABASE_MATCH",
          "source": "CultureBotHT",
          "notes": "Imported from CultureBotHT. CAS-RN 1040352-40-6 present, but no CHEBI entry exists (checked OAK CHEBI sqlite + PubChem CID synonyms). Curator can promote to a CHEBI primary if/when CHEBI adds the term."
        },
        {
          "evidence_type": "DATABASE_MATCH",
          "source": "anchor_cas_hydrate_records",
          "notes": "2-Keto-D-gluconic acid hemicalcium salt hydrate is a hydrate/salt with its own CAS and no exact ChEBI term; anchored to the parent CHEBI:27469 '2-dehydro-D-gluconic acid' by narrowMatch per MAPPING_SEMANTICS.md Section 3 step 2. hemicalcium salt hydrate of 2-dehydro-D-gluconic acid"
        },
        {
          "evidence_type": "DATABASE_MATCH",
          "source": "MIM curation (#342)",
          "notes": "mapping_quality NARROW_MATCH -> CLOSE_MATCH, predicate skos:narrowMatch -> skos:closeMatch. narrowMatch asserts this record is *narrower in meaning* than CHEBI:27469 ('2-dehydro-D-gluconic acid') — a subsumption ChEBI itself denies: it files hydrates under CHEBI:35505 'hydrate', never under the anhydrous compound, which is not an ancestor even transitively. A hydrate is a distinct substance containing the anhydrous form, not a specialization of it. closeMatch claims similarity without subsumption. The ontology_id and the record's own identifier are unchanged."
        },
        {
          "evidence_type": "MANUAL_CURATION",
          "source": "MIM Step7d scientific review (#901)",
          "notes": "CAS1040352-40-6 and K6250 source name agree on hemicalcium salt hydrate with unspecified xH2O. Keep distinct from the separately curated monohydrate/MPBio owner. Keep CHEBI27469 acid as the verified available parent for salt/hydrate grounding; do not select CHEBI3309 calcium gluconate, which lacks the keto group. Own CAS remains exact; B1 local identity is generated separately. Only CAS and source provenance are active. PubChem's fixed-water representation is not enough to backfill a stoichiometric formula/structure against supplier xH2O. Primary source references: https://www.sigmaaldrich.com/US/en/product/sigma/k6250; https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/rest/pug/substance/sourceid/Sigma-Aldrich/K6250_SIGMA/JSON; https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/rest/pug/compound/name/1040352-40-6/property/Title,MolecularFormula,MolecularWeight,InChI,InChIKey,CanonicalSMILES/JSON; https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/backend/api/public/compound/27469/. Captures, exact input hashes and scope limits: reports/step7d_mapping_901_20261103/evidence-manifest.json. This curation adds no scientific, mapping-release or role approval; changed owner bytes withdraw inherited support."
        }
      ]
    },
