    "owner_mim_id": "MIM:0000475",
    "owner_primary_identifier": "cas:154804-51-0",
    "owner_grounding": {
      "ontology_id": "CHEBI:132089",
      "ontology_label": "sodium glycerol 2-phosphate",
      "ontology_source": "CHEBI",
      "mapping_quality": "NARROW_MATCH",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "evidence_type": "DATABASE_MATCH",
          "source": "CultureBotHT",
          "notes": "Imported from CultureBotHT. CAS-RN 154804-51-0 present, but no CHEBI entry exists (checked OAK CHEBI sqlite + PubChem CID synonyms). Curator can promote to a CHEBI primary if/when CHEBI adds the term."
        },
        {
          "evidence_type": "DATABASE_MATCH",
          "source": "anchor_cas_hydrate_records",
          "notes": "Beta-Glycerophosphate disodium salt hydrate is a hydrate/salt with its own CAS and no exact ChEBI term; anchored to the parent CHEBI:17270 'glycerol 2-phosphate' by narrowMatch per MAPPING_SEMANTICS.md Section 3 step 2. disodium salt hydrate of glycerol 2-phosphate"
        },
        {
          "evidence_type": "DATABASE_MATCH",
          "source": "MIM curation (#342)",
          "notes": "mapping_quality NARROW_MATCH -> CLOSE_MATCH, predicate skos:narrowMatch -> skos:closeMatch. narrowMatch asserts this record is *narrower in meaning* than CHEBI:17270 ('glycerol 2-phosphate') — a subsumption ChEBI itself denies: it files hydrates under CHEBI:35505 'hydrate', never under the anhydrous compound, which is not an ancestor even transitively. A hydrate is a distinct substance containing the anhydrous form, not a specialization of it. closeMatch claims similarity without subsumption. The ontology_id and the record's own identifier are unchanged."
        },
        {
          "evidence_type": "MANUAL_CURATION",
          "source": "MIM Step7d scientific review (#901)",
          "notes": "CAS154804-51-0 denotes beta/2-glycerophosphate disodium hydrate in the inspected supplier comparator and historical source label. Preserve this hydrate owner separately from CHEBI132089 sodium beta-glycerophosphate and the distinct fixed-water sibling. CHEBI132089 sodium glycerol2-phosphate is a closer verified parent than free-acid CHEBI17270: its definition is the disodium salt. Use NARROW_MATCH/broadMatch to132089, not exact identity and not tetrahydrate132092. Current CID44828775/SMILES/InChI place negative charge on terminal alcohols while leaving phosphate OH, and all current structure/formula fields impose one water. Supplier comparator instead gives phosphate disodium salt xH2O. Withdraw formula, SMILES, InChI and CID without guessing a replacement. Primary source references: https://www.sigmaaldrich.com/US/en/product/sigma/g9422; https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/rest/pug/substance/sourceid/Sigma-Aldrich/G9422_SIGMA/JSON; https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/rest/pug/compound/name/154804-51-0/property/Title,MolecularFormula,MolecularWeight,InChI,InChIKey,CanonicalSMILES/JSON; https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/backend/api/public/compound/17270/; https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/backend/api/public/compound/132089/; https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/backend/api/public/compound/132092/. Captures, exact input hashes and scope limits: reports/step7d_mapping_901_20261103/evidence-manifest.json. This curation adds no scientific, mapping-release or role approval; changed owner bytes withdraw inherited support."
        }
      ]
    },
