          "notes": "Corrected mis-mapping: auto-created from CultureBotHT CAS-RN 461-05-2, which in ChEBI genuinely resolves to CHEBI:48601 (carnitinamide chloride — the amide, C7H17N2O2·Cl), not carnitine. Remapped to the carnitine parent CHEBI:17126 as a NARROW_MATCH (salt/hydrochloride -> parent), mirroring sibling Carnitine_Dl_Hydrochloride. Erroneous cas_rn 461-05-2 and amide chemistry backfill removed."
        },
        {
          "evidence_type": "DATABASE_MATCH",
          "source": "https://api-evsrest.nci.nih.gov/api/v1/concept/ncit/C216679?include=full",
          "notes": "Supersedes prior identity interpretation without erasing it. NCI EVS NCIt 26.10d NCIT:C216679 'DL-Carnitine Hydrochloride' is active, CAS 461-05-2, UNII F64264D63N: https://api-evsrest.nci.nih.gov/api/v1/concept/ncit/C216679?include=full. PubChem CID 5970 supplies chloride-bearing C7H16ClNO3 chemistry, 197.66 g/mol: https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/5970. CHEBI:48601 is the distinct carnitinamide chloride despite its conflicting CAS cross-reference: https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI:48601. Inspected 2026-11-01; hash-bound captures and retrieval receipts: reports/carnitine_hydrochloride_1004_20261101/sources/manifest.json (sha256 d5bf100092c4a16d29552e79475b1a8a8891a797c046377365a46f0fb85ce911). Sigma C9500 supplier evidence supports the original racemate. CultureBotHT raw CSV is a hash-bound local snapshot associated with checkout context, not a commit-attested blob. Direct CAS API returned 401; no CAS Registry verification is claimed. Historical CHEBI/KG source tokens are retained provenance, not independent support for the NCIT identity. Approved decision: https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1004#issuecomment-6555569867. No scientific/release approval is asserted."
        }
      ]
    },
