    "owner_grounding": {
      "ontology_id": "CHEBI:31380",
      "ontology_label": "Cefsulodin sodium",
      "ontology_source": "CHEBI",
      "mapping_quality": "NARROW_MATCH",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "evidence_type": "DATABASE_MATCH",
          "source": "CultureBotHT",
          "notes": "Imported from CultureBotHT. CAS-RN→CHEBI mapping resolved via OAK CHEBI sqlite (cas xref). FEBA/Hans80 panels: Hans80metals."
        },
        {
          "evidence_type": "DATABASE_MATCH",
          "source": "MIM curation (#321/#334)",
          "notes": "identifier CHEBI:31380 -> kgmicrobe.compound:cefsulodin_sodium_salt_hydrate; mapping_quality EXACT_MATCH -> NARROW_MATCH. The record is a hydrate of CHEBI:31380 ('Cefsulodin sodium') and was sharing that term's identifier — the identity collapse MAPPING_SEMANTICS §3 forbids, which made a distinct substance indistinguishable from its anhydrous parent downstream. ChEBI has no term for this hydrate and the record carries no verified CAS, so steps 1 and 2 are unavailable and step 3 applies."
        },
        {
          "evidence_type": "DATABASE_MATCH",
          "source": "MIM curation (#342)",
          "notes": "mapping_quality NARROW_MATCH -> CLOSE_MATCH, predicate skos:narrowMatch -> skos:closeMatch. narrowMatch asserts this record is *narrower in meaning* than CHEBI:31380 ('Cefsulodin sodium') — a subsumption ChEBI itself denies: it files hydrates under CHEBI:35505 'hydrate', never under the anhydrous compound, which is not an ancestor even transitively. A hydrate is a distinct substance containing the anhydrous form, not a specialization of it. closeMatch claims similarity without subsumption. The ontology_id and the record's own identifier are unchanged."
        },
        {
          "evidence_type": "MANUAL_CURATION",
          "source": "MIM Step7d scientific review (#901)",
          "notes": "Historical C8145 and current supplier describe the same source-defined cefsulodin sodium salt hydrate xH2O. Retain local hydrate identity; CAS52152-93-9 resolves to the water-free salt and is not selected as exact hydrate primary. CHEBI31380 is the verified water-free sodium salt and the closest inspected parent. NARROW_MATCH exports broadMatch; do not select NCITC98228 as exact hydrate because it describes the same water-free salt. Dry structures were already removed in7b. Move the remaining procurement CAS out of unqualified chemical_properties.cas_rn into supplied_form; preserve source/retrieval metadata and full old history. Primary source references: https://www.sigmaaldrich.com/US/en/product/sigma/c8145; https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/rest/pug/substance/sourceid/Sigma-Aldrich/C8145_SIGMA/JSON; https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/rest/pug/compound/name/52152-93-9/property/Title,MolecularFormula,MolecularWeight,InChI,InChIKey,CanonicalSMILES/JSON; https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/backend/api/public/compound/31380/. Captures, exact input hashes and scope limits: reports/step7d_mapping_901_20261103/evidence-manifest.json. This curation adds no scientific, mapping-release or role approval; changed owner bytes withdraw inherited support."
        }
      ]
    },
