    "owner_sha256": "0ce7850b4cf8f931bdb93e8a40c7262f7ad665d30cd259f99fc03ec1931a9443",
    "owner_mim_id": "MIM:0000680",
    "owner_primary_identifier": "kgmicrobe.compound:chlorhexidine_diacetate_salt_hydrate",
    "owner_grounding": {
      "ontology_id": "CHEBI:81711",
      "ontology_label": "chlorhexidine acetate",
      "ontology_source": "CHEBI",
      "mapping_quality": "NARROW_MATCH",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "evidence_type": "DATABASE_MATCH",
          "source": "CultureBotHT",
          "notes": "Imported from CultureBotHT. CAS-RN→CHEBI mapping resolved via OAK CHEBI sqlite (cas xref). FEBA/Hans80 panels: Hans80Anti, Hans80metals."
        },
        {
          "evidence_type": "DATABASE_MATCH",
          "source": "MIM curation (#321/#334)",
          "notes": "identifier CHEBI:81711 -> kgmicrobe.compound:chlorhexidine_diacetate_salt_hydrate; mapping_quality EXACT_MATCH -> NARROW_MATCH. The record is a hydrate of CHEBI:81711 ('chlorhexidine acetate') and was sharing that term's identifier — the identity collapse MAPPING_SEMANTICS §3 forbids, which made a distinct substance indistinguishable from its anhydrous parent downstream. ChEBI has no term for this hydrate and the record carries no verified CAS, so steps 1 and 2 are unavailable and step 3 applies."
        },
        {
          "evidence_type": "DATABASE_MATCH",
          "source": "MIM curation (#342)",
          "notes": "mapping_quality NARROW_MATCH -> CLOSE_MATCH, predicate skos:narrowMatch -> skos:closeMatch. narrowMatch asserts this record is *narrower in meaning* than CHEBI:81711 ('chlorhexidine acetate') — a subsumption ChEBI itself denies: it files hydrates under CHEBI:35505 'hydrate', never under the anhydrous compound, which is not an ancestor even transitively. A hydrate is a distinct substance containing the anhydrous form, not a specialization of it. closeMatch claims similarity without subsumption. The ontology_id and the record's own identifier are unchanged."
        },
        {
          "evidence_type": "MANUAL_CURATION",
          "source": "MIM Step7d scientific review (#901)",
          "notes": "Historical C6143 and current supplier explicitly identify chlorhexidine diacetate salt hydrate, current formula xH2O. This settles the source-defined variable hydrate, not a fixed monohydrate. Retain its local identity distinct from water-free CHEBI81711. Use NARROW_MATCH/broadMatch to the diacetate parent. Current supplier CAS206986-79-0 yields mixed PubChem forms and does not justify any exact CAS or ontology primary promotion. 7b removed dry structures. Historical chemical CAS56-95-1 is the water-free parent CAS; move procurement context to supplied_form with explicit historical/current disagreement, preserving both observations without exact-identity assertion. Primary source references: https://www.sigmaaldrich.com/US/en/product/sigma/c6143; https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/rest/pug/substance/sourceid/Sigma-Aldrich/C6143_SIGMA/JSON; https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/rest/pug/compound/name/56-95-1/property/Title,MolecularFormula,MolecularWeight,InChI,InChIKey,CanonicalSMILES/JSON; https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/rest/pug/compound/name/206986-79-0/property/Title,MolecularFormula,InChI,InChIKey/JSON; https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/backend/api/public/compound/81711/. Captures, exact input hashes and scope limits: reports/step7d_mapping_901_20261103/evidence-manifest.json. Independent review identifies the existing exact synonym 'N,N''''-hexane-1,6-diylbis[N'-(4-chlorophenyl)triimidodicarbonic diamide] acetate (1:2)' as the water-free parent, not this hydrate; preserve it as REJECTED_LABEL. This curation adds no scientific, mapping-release or role approval; changed owner bytes withdraw inherited support."
        }
      ]
    },
