    "entry_id": "row-000851",
    "selection_entry_sha256": "a0e3dd00e9ae04901064040095f806850dfbf1ea7852e124ce07d3d2ca5039f3",
    "candidate_position": 851,
    "before_position": 842,
    "class": "matched",
    "owner": "data/ingredients/mapped/Cu_No32_X_3_H2o.yaml",
    "owner_sha256": "8a5ae39854c539aa23ed4f54a85bed3c254e73de141f8dda5817005a9560502d",
    "owner_mim_id": "MIM:0000773",
    "owner_primary_identifier": "cas:10031-43-3",
    "owner_grounding": {
      "ontology_id": "CHEBI:78036",
      "ontology_label": "copper(II) nitrate",
      "ontology_source": "CHEBI",
      "mapping_quality": "NARROW_MATCH",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "evidence_type": "DATABASE_MATCH",
          "source": "CultureMech",
          "notes": "[HISTORICAL — superseded by the #321 re-grade below: this record is a hydrate of CHEBI:78036, not an exact match to it] Imported from CultureMech pipeline, quality=DIRECT_MATCH"
        },
        {
          "evidence_type": "DATABASE_MATCH",
          "source": "MIM curation (#321/#334)",
          "notes": "identifier CHEBI:78036 -> kgmicrobe.compound:cu_no32_x_3_h2o; mapping_quality EXACT_MATCH -> NARROW_MATCH. The record is a hydrate of CHEBI:78036 ('copper(II) nitrate') and was sharing that term's identifier — the identity collapse MAPPING_SEMANTICS §3 forbids, which made a distinct substance indistinguishable from its anhydrous parent downstream. ChEBI has no term for this hydrate and the record carries no verified CAS, so steps 1 and 2 are unavailable and step 3 applies."
        },
        {
          "evidence_type": "DATABASE_MATCH",
          "source": "MIM curation (#321)",
          "notes": "molecular_formula 'Cu.2NO3' -> 'Cu.2NO3.3H2O'. The recorded value described the anhydrous salt while the label names a hydrate, understating the mass by 18 g/mol per water. Corrected because the label states 3 water(s) of hydration, and the recorded formula was byte-identical to the anhydrous parent CHEBI:78036's ChEBI formula ('Cu.2NO3') — the mark of a value inherited from the parent rather than measured for this record. Water appended in ChEBI's own dot-separated notation."
        },
        {
          "evidence_type": "DATABASE_MATCH",
          "source": "MIM curation (#342)",
          "notes": "mapping_quality NARROW_MATCH -> CLOSE_MATCH, predicate skos:narrowMatch -> skos:closeMatch. narrowMatch asserts this record is *narrower in meaning* than CHEBI:78036 ('copper(II) nitrate') — a subsumption ChEBI itself denies: it files hydrates under CHEBI:35505 'hydrate', never under the anhydrous compound, which is not an ancestor even transitively. A hydrate is a distinct substance containing the anhydrous form, not a specialization of it. closeMatch claims similarity without subsumption. The ontology_id and the record's own identifier are unchanged."
        },
        {
          "evidence_type": "MANUAL_CURATION",
          "source": "MIM Step7d scientific review (#901)",
          "notes": "Historical source, current formula and independent GSRS/PubChem agree on copper(II) nitrate trihydrate CAS10031-43-3. The ignored-inclusive owner scan found no other current owner of this CAS. Promote local primary to cas:10031-43-3, retain existing local registry identity, and NARROW_MATCH/broadMatch CHEBI78036. No exact eligible CHEBI/NCIT trihydrate term was established by the bounded queries. Keep CAS and Cu.2NO3.3H2O. Do not automatically add CID/SMILES/InChI from the reviewed comparator. Primary source references: https://gsrs.ncats.nih.gov/api/v1/substances/066PG1506T?view=full; https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/rest/pug/compound/name/10031-43-3/property/Title,MolecularFormula,MolecularWeight,InChI,InChIKey,CanonicalSMILES/JSON; https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/backend/api/public/compound/78036/. Captures, exact input hashes and scope limits: reports/step7d_mapping_901_20261103/evidence-manifest.json. Independent review identifies the existing exact synonym 'copper(2+) dinitrate' as the water-free parent, not this hydrate; preserve it as REJECTED_LABEL. This curation adds no scientific, mapping-release or role approval; changed owner bytes withdraw inherited support."
        }
      ]
    },
