      "evidence": [
        {
          "evidence_type": "DATABASE_MATCH",
          "source": "CultureMech",
          "notes": "SUPERSEDED (#312): Imported from CultureMech pipeline, quality=DIRECT_MATCH"
        },
        {
          "evidence_type": "DATABASE_MATCH",
          "source": "MIM curation (#321)",
          "notes": "molecular_formula 'Cu.O4S' -> 'Cu.O4S.2H2O'. The recorded value described the anhydrous salt while the label names a hydrate, understating the mass by 18 g/mol per water. Corrected because the label states 2 water(s) of hydration, and the recorded formula was byte-identical to the anhydrous parent CHEBI:23414's ChEBI formula ('Cu.O4S') — the mark of a value inherited from the parent rather than measured for this record. Water appended in ChEBI's own dot-separated notation."
        },
        {
          "evidence_type": "MANUAL_CURATION",
          "source": "MIM curation (#312); chebi.db",
          "notes": "identifier CHEBI:23414 -> kgmicrobe.compound:cuso4_x_2_h2o; ontology CHEBI:23414 ('copper(II) sulfate') -> CHEBI:23414 ('copper(II) sulfate'); mapping_quality SYNONYM_MATCH -> CLOSE_MATCH. CuSO4 x 2 H2O is a MediaDive label for a hydration state no source verifies (hydrate_review: WRONG_TERM_ANHYDROUS, 'Probably CuSO4 x 5 H2O; phase studies establish the pentahydrate'). It shared CHEBI:23414 with the anhydrous CuSO4 record; the 2026-08-10 regrade to SYNONYM_MATCH still published exactMatch. The #344 malformed-hydrate shape: local identity, closeMatch to the anhydrous parent, chemistry blank, anhydrous aliases REJECTED_LABEL, memberships only for recipes whose source label names this row ('CuSO4 x 2 H2O', 'CuSO4 . 2H2O')."
        }
      ]
    },
