          "notes": "Parent class identified via pubchem-xref; matched_via='pubchem CID 22812950'"
        },
        {
          "evidence_type": "DATABASE_MATCH",
          "source": "MIM curation (#342)",
          "notes": "mapping_quality NARROW_MATCH -> CLOSE_MATCH, predicate skos:narrowMatch -> skos:closeMatch. narrowMatch asserts this record is *narrower in meaning* than CHEBI:190546 ('D-Fructose 6-Phosphate-Disodium Salt') — a subsumption ChEBI itself denies: it files hydrates under CHEBI:35505 'hydrate', never under the anhydrous compound, which is not an ancestor even transitively. A hydrate is a distinct substance containing the anhydrous form, not a specialization of it. closeMatch claims similarity without subsumption. The ontology_id and the record's own identifier are unchanged."
        },
        {
          "evidence_type": "MANUAL_CURATION",
          "source": "MIM Step7d scientific review (#901)",
          "notes": "Catalogue line1360 names the disodium D-fructose6-phosphate hydrate and CAS26177-86-6. Inspected supplier F3627 independently uses that CAS and C6H11Na2O9P·xH2O. No fixed water count is justified. The ChEBI parent is the two-sodium water-free moiety; retain the CAS identity and use a form-of broadMatch, never an exact hydrate-to-parent assertion. See the complete identity, mapping, chemistry and synonym assessment in reports/step7d_mapping_901_20261103/authors/science-b/full-assessments.json; owner selector data/ingredients/mapped/D-Fructose_6-phosphate_Disodium_Salt_Hydrate.yaml. Primary source references: https://github.com/CultureBotAI/CultureBotHT; https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/backend/api/public/compound/190546/; https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/rest/pug/compound/name/26177-86-6/property/MolecularFormula,MolecularWeight,InChI,InChIKey,IUPACName/JSON; https://www.sigmaaldrich.com/US/en/product/sigma/f3627. Captures, exact input hashes and scope limits: reports/step7d_mapping_901_20261103/evidence-manifest.json. This curation adds no scientific, mapping-release or role approval; changed owner bytes withdraw inherited support."
        }
      ]
