    "owner_sha256": "1847afa09068731812855c066cf9457bf9eb609aa105c8ed6c97790bd2ea8072",
    "owner_mim_id": "MIM:0000823",
    "owner_primary_identifier": "NCIT:C80300",
    "owner_grounding": {
      "ontology_id": "NCIT:C80300",
      "ontology_label": "Maltose Monohydrate",
      "ontology_source": "NCIT",
      "mapping_quality": "CAS_RN_LOOKUP",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "evidence_type": "DATABASE_MATCH",
          "source": "CultureBotHT",
          "notes": "Imported from CultureBotHT. CAS-RN 6363-53-7 present, but no CHEBI entry exists for the monohydrate specifically (checked OAK CHEBI sqlite + PubChem CID synonyms). FEBA/Hans80 panels: FEBA_carbon. Used in 9 CultureBot media; samples: Mega, ZMB Gut, SGW Northen Exometabolite mix 5x…. Curator can promote to a CHEBI primary if/when CHEBI adds D-maltose monohydrate."
        },
        {
          "evidence_type": "MANUAL_REVIEW",
          "source": "family_mismatch_fix",
          "notes": "fix(family-mismatch): was CHEBI:233428 (5-(N-ethyl-N-isopropyl) amiloride) from a stale pubchem-xref hit on PubChem CID 23615261; the bogus CHEBI was removed from the published SSSOM in PR #2 / commit 887ee9f and the ontology_mapping is now retargeted at CHEBI:17306 (maltose) as the correct narrowMatch parent. D-Maltose monohydrate is a hydrate of D-maltose, which has no separate CHEBI; maltose (CHEBI:17306) is the closest available parent."
        },
        {
          "evidence_type": "DATABASE_MATCH",
          "source": "MIM curation (#342)",
          "notes": "mapping_quality NARROW_MATCH -> CLOSE_MATCH, predicate skos:narrowMatch -> skos:closeMatch. narrowMatch asserts this record is *narrower in meaning* than CHEBI:17306 ('maltose') — a subsumption ChEBI itself denies: it files hydrates under CHEBI:35505 'hydrate', never under the anhydrous compound, which is not an ancestor even transitively. A hydrate is a distinct substance containing the anhydrous form, not a specialization of it. closeMatch claims similarity without subsumption. The ontology_id and the record's own identifier are unchanged."
        },
        {
          "evidence_type": "MANUAL_CURATION",
          "source": "MIM Step7d scientific review (#901)",
          "notes": "Resolve #1117 for this owner to NCIT:C80300, Maltose Monohydrate, using CAS_RN_LOOKUP as method provenance. The archived catalogue explicitly selects SigmaM5885/CAS6363-53-7/360.31; the inspected official M5885 specification confirms CAS and C12H22O11·H2O. NCIt links this CAS to UNIIDM477EE40D; the GSRS PRIMARY record explicitly cross-links C80300, CAS6363-53-7, D-(+)-MALTOSE MONOHYDRATE and beta naming, and PubChem23615261. The open-chain representation and beta synonym occur in that same registry identity; §3 readability/orderability supports the readable monohydrate node, without choosing a different anomer from lexical resemblance. Keep generic Maltose_Hydrate separate. See the complete identity, mapping, chemistry and synonym assessment in reports/step7d_mapping_901_20261103/authors/science-b/full-assessments.json; owner selector data/ingredients/mapped/D-Maltose_Monohydrate.yaml. Primary source references: https://github.com/CultureBotAI/CultureBotHT; https://api-evsrest.nci.nih.gov/api/v1/concept/ncit/C80300?include=full; https://gsrs.ncats.nih.gov/api/v1/substances/DM477EE40D?view=full; https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/rest/pug/compound/cid/23615261/property/MolecularFormula,InChI,InChIKey/JSON; https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/rest/pug/compound/name/6363-53-7/property/MolecularFormula,MolecularWeight,InChI,InChIKey,IUPACName/JSON; https://www.sigmaaldrich.com/specification-sheets/677/787/M5885-BULK________SIAL_____.pdf. Captures, exact input hashes and scope limits: reports/step7d_mapping_901_20261103/evidence-manifest.json. This curation adds no scientific, mapping-release or role approval; changed owner bytes withdraw inherited support."
        }
      ]
    },
