      "evidence": [
        {
          "evidence_type": "MANUAL_CURATION",
          "source": "MIM curation (#260)",
          "notes": "Created to cover a CultureMech label MIM could not resolve (#260): ChEBI has no racemic tyrosine term — a search returns only derivatives (DL-tyrosine betaine, racemetirosine) — so the stereo-unspecified parent is the closest available, which is what the corpus's other 15 `DL-` records do (DL-aspartic acid->CHEBI:22660, DL-methionine->CHEBI:16811). Graded CLOSE_MATCH, not the EXACT those often use: the label names a racemate and the term does not distinguish stereochemistry at all, so skos:closeMatch is the honest predicate. NOT CHEBI:17895 L-tyrosine, which is what CultureMech asserts (CultureMech#276) — that silently discards the D-enantiomer."
        }
      ]
    },
