    "owner_mim_id": "MIM:0000997",
    "owner_primary_identifier": "cas:13235-36-4",
    "owner_grounding": {
      "ontology_id": "CHEBI:750784",
      "ontology_label": "edetate sodium",
      "ontology_source": "CHEBI",
      "mapping_quality": "NARROW_MATCH",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "evidence_type": "DATABASE_MATCH",
          "source": "CultureBotHT",
          "notes": "Imported from CultureBotHT. CAS-RN 13235-36-4 present, but no CHEBI entry exists (checked OAK CHEBI sqlite + PubChem CID synonyms). Used in 4 CultureBot media; samples: MME noCarbon, MTM noNitrogen noCarbon, MME noNitrogen noCarbon…. Curator can promote to a CHEBI primary if/when CHEBI adds the term."
        },
        {
          "evidence_type": "DATABASE_MATCH",
          "source": "anchor_cas_hydrate_records",
          "notes": "EDTA tetrasodium tetrahydrate salt is a hydrate/salt with its own CAS and no exact ChEBI term; anchored to the parent CHEBI:4735 'ethylenediaminetetraacetic acid' by narrowMatch per MAPPING_SEMANTICS.md Section 3 step 2. tetrasodium tetrahydrate salt of EDTA"
        },
        {
          "evidence_type": "DATABASE_MATCH",
          "source": "MIM curation (#342)",
          "notes": "mapping_quality NARROW_MATCH -> CLOSE_MATCH, predicate skos:narrowMatch -> skos:closeMatch. narrowMatch asserts this record is *narrower in meaning* than CHEBI:4735 ('ethylenediaminetetraacetic acid') — a subsumption ChEBI itself denies: it files hydrates under CHEBI:35505 'hydrate', never under the anhydrous compound, which is not an ancestor even transitively. A hydrate is a distinct substance containing the anhydrous form, not a specialization of it. closeMatch claims similarity without subsumption. The ontology_id and the record's own identifier are unchanged."
        },
        {
          "evidence_type": "MANUAL_CURATION",
          "source": "MIM Step7d scientific review (#901)",
          "notes": "Catalogue line1092/CAS13235-36-4/FW452.23 and PubChemCID23287279 consistently specify EDTA tetrasodium tetrahydrate. No exact hydrate term found in the bounded searches. CHEBI750784 edetate sodium is a closer parent than EDTA freeacidCHEBI4735: it explicitly has four sodium ions and no water, with matching organic skeleton. NCItC76598 independently describes that water-free tetrasodium parent/CAS64-02-8. Retain hydrate CAS and broadMatch to CHEBI750784. See the complete identity, mapping, chemistry and synonym assessment in reports/step7d_mapping_901_20261103/authors/science-b/full-assessments.json; owner selector data/ingredients/mapped/EDTA_Tetrasodium_Tetrahydrate_Salt.yaml. Primary source references: https://github.com/CultureBotAI/CultureBotHT; https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/rest/pug/compound/name/13235-36-4/property/MolecularFormula,MolecularWeight,InChI,InChIKey,IUPACName/JSON; https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/backend/api/public/compound/750784/; https://api-evsrest.nci.nih.gov/api/v1/concept/ncit/C76598?include=full; https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/backend/api/public/compound/4735/. Captures, exact input hashes and scope limits: reports/step7d_mapping_901_20261103/evidence-manifest.json. This curation adds no scientific, mapping-release or role approval; changed owner bytes withdraw inherited support."
        }
      ]
    },
