          "source": "MIM curation (#321)",
          "notes": "molecular_formula 'C26H43NO6' -> 'C26H45NO7'. The record's own CAS 1192657-83-2 resolves in PubChem to a title matching the label verbatim ('Glycocholic acid hydrate') with formula C26H45NO7 — exactly one H2O more than the recorded value. **Two authorities disagree here and the divergence is deliberate**: the mapped term CHEBI:182320, whose own label is 'Glycocholic acid hydrate', records the *anhydrous* C26H43NO6, so after this change the record no longer matches its EXACT_MATCH term's formula. PubChem is preferred because its value is tied to the specific registered substance this record's CAS denotes, whereas ChEBI carrying an anhydrous formula on a term it names a hydrate is the same modelling gap as #342. Flagged rather than hidden: if #342 concludes ChEBI's hydrate handling should be taken at face value, this record should revert."
        }
      ]
    },
