          "source": "Edison LITERATURE (PaperQA3) + local CHEBI verification",
          "notes": "Potassium phosphite monobasic, KH2PO3. A culture-medium method quoted in the report names it with supplier and CAS RN 13977-65-6, used to replace dipotassium phosphate in phosphorus-modified BG-11. The report states the number should be stored as registry grounding and not presented as an ontology CURIE. CHEBI:44976 phosphonic acid is the parent acid; this record is its monopotassium salt."
        }
      ]
    },
