        },
        {
          "evidence_type": "DATABASE_MATCH",
          "source": "CHEBI via OLS (stem-substring)",
          "notes": "Parent class identified via stem-substring; matched_via='L-Aspartic acid sodium salt monohydrate'"
        },
        {
          "evidence_type": "DATABASE_MATCH",
          "source": "MIM curation (#342)",
          "notes": "mapping_quality NARROW_MATCH -> CLOSE_MATCH, predicate skos:narrowMatch -> skos:closeMatch. narrowMatch asserts this record is *narrower in meaning* than CHEBI:17053 ('L-aspartic acid') — a subsumption ChEBI itself denies: it files hydrates under CHEBI:35505 'hydrate', never under the anhydrous compound, which is not an ancestor even transitively. A hydrate is a distinct substance containing the anhydrous form, not a specialization of it. closeMatch claims similarity without subsumption. The ontology_id and the record's own identifier are unchanged."
        },
        {
          "evidence_type": "MANUAL_CURATION",
          "source": "MIM Step7d scientific review (#901)",
          "notes": "Catalogueline1340 CAS323194-76-9/FW173.1 names sodium L-aspartate monohydrate; PubChemCID23679051 gives one sodium, one water and Lconfiguration. No exacthydrate or nearer sodium-aspartate term found in bounded CHEBI/NCIT label/synonym/CAS searches. Retain CAS and broadMatch to L-asparticacidCHEBI17053 with separate B1 registry. See the complete identity, mapping, chemistry and synonym assessment in reports/step7d_mapping_901_20261103/authors/science-b/full-assessments.json; owner selector data/ingredients/mapped/L-Aspartic_Acid_Sodium_Salt_Monohydrate.yaml. Primary source references: https://github.com/CultureBotAI/CultureBotHT; https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/rest/pug/compound/name/323194-76-9/property/MolecularFormula,MolecularWeight,InChI,InChIKey,IUPACName/JSON; https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/backend/api/public/compound/17053/. Captures, exact input hashes and scope limits: reports/step7d_mapping_901_20261103/evidence-manifest.json. This curation adds no scientific, mapping-release or role approval; changed owner bytes withdraw inherited support."
        }
      ]
    },
