          "notes": "Remapped from mesh:D013025 \"Soybeans\" (a source-organism stand-in) to the chemical class CHEBI:28874 \"phosphatidylinositol\" (any glycerophosphoinositol with one phosphatidyl group esterified to inositol). The commercial product is a natural soybean PI mixture, so the generic class is the correct grounding rather than a single PI species (e.g. CHEBI:136245 \"phosphatidylinositol 36:1\"); the term is broader than the ingredient → BROAD_MATCH. Mirrors the sibling L-alpha-Phosphatidylcholine → CHEBI:86658 mapping. identifier kept as cas:97281-52-2 (class match is not exact, so not promoted to a CHEBI primary)."
        }
      ]
