          "source": "MIM curation (#342)",
          "notes": "mapping_quality NARROW_MATCH -> CLOSE_MATCH, predicate skos:narrowMatch -> skos:closeMatch. narrowMatch asserts this record is *narrower in meaning* than CHEBI:64736 ('magnesium nitrate') — a subsumption ChEBI itself denies: it files hydrates under CHEBI:35505 'hydrate', never under the anhydrous compound, which is not an ancestor even transitively. A hydrate is a distinct substance containing the anhydrous form, not a specialization of it. closeMatch claims similarity without subsumption. The ontology_id and the record's own identifier are unchanged."
        },
        {
          "evidence_type": "MANUAL_CURATION",
          "source": "MIM Step7d scientific review (#901)",
          "notes": "MediaDiveingredient1763 explicitly names Mg(NO3)2 x6H2O and CAS13446-18-9; freshPubChemCAS resolvesCID202877 with magnesium dinitrate hexahydrate/H12MgN2O12. ParentCHEBI64736 is magnesium nitrate withoutwaters. No exacteligiblehydrate candidatefound. RetainformCAS and broadMatch toparent with B1registry; no inventedchemicalprops. See the complete identity, mapping, chemistry and synonym assessment in reports/step7d_mapping_901_20261103/authors/science-b/full-assessments.json; owner selector data/ingredients/mapped/Magnesium_Nitrate_Hexahydrate.yaml. Primary source references: https://github.com/CultureBotAI/CultureBotHT; https://mediadive.dsmz.de/rest/ingredients; https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/rest/pug/compound/name/13446-18-9/property/MolecularFormula,MolecularWeight,InChI,InChIKey,IUPACName/JSON; https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/backend/api/public/compound/64736/. Captures, exact input hashes and scope limits: reports/step7d_mapping_901_20261103/evidence-manifest.json. This curation adds no scientific, mapping-release or role approval; changed owner bytes withdraw inherited support."
        }
      ]
