          "source": "MIM curation (#213)",
          "notes": "Maltose hydrate is the hydrated form of maltose. CHEBI has anhydrous maltose CHEBI:17306 but no hydrate term; Section 3 mint + narrowMatch, per the hydrate convention in #242 (#213)."
        },
        {
          "evidence_type": "DATABASE_MATCH",
          "source": "MIM curation (#342)",
          "notes": "mapping_quality NARROW_MATCH -> CLOSE_MATCH, predicate skos:narrowMatch -> skos:closeMatch. narrowMatch asserts this record is *narrower in meaning* than CHEBI:17306 ('maltose') — a subsumption ChEBI itself denies: it files hydrates under CHEBI:35505 'hydrate', never under the anhydrous compound, which is not an ancestor even transitively. A hydrate is a distinct substance containing the anhydrous form, not a specialization of it. closeMatch claims similarity without subsumption. The ontology_id and the record's own identifier are unchanged."
        },
        {
          "evidence_type": "MANUAL_CURATION",
          "source": "MIM Step7d scientific review (#901)",
          "notes": "The source table explicitly names maltose hydrate and8BacDive-metabolite-utilization observations. Preserve its distinct local identity without assigning the separate D-maltose-monohydrate CAS or an anomer. See the complete identity, mapping, chemistry and synonym assessment in reports/step7d_mapping_901_20261103/authors/science-c/assessments-v2.json; owner selector data/ingredients/mapped/Maltose_Hydrate.yaml. Primary source references: https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/backend/api/public/compound/17306/; https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/api/search?q=Maltose%20Hydrate&ontology=chebi,ncit&rows=100; https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/blob/467aa319a06ef992035f509f66fe251082b44ae1/data/custom/microbedecoder/unmapped_labels.tsv. Captures, exact input hashes and scope limits: reports/step7d_mapping_901_20261103/evidence-manifest.json. This curation adds no scientific, mapping-release or role approval; changed owner bytes withdraw inherited support."
        }
      ]
    },
