          "notes": "Added 'Defibrinated rabbit blood' as a RELATED_SYNONYM (#260): MICRO has `defibrinated sheep blood` and `defibrinated horse blood` as classes but no rabbit equivalent, and MICRO:0001229 `rabbit blood` is already held here. So unlike its sheep and horse siblings this one cannot become a record — the granularity available in the ontology decides. CultureMech uses this surface form and label_index did not contain it, so the lookup missed. No new record: MICRO:0001229 is this record's identifier, and in MIM the identifier IS the ontology CURIE, so a second record on it would be a duplicate primary key rather than added coverage."
