      "evidence": [
        {
          "evidence_type": "DATABASE_MATCH",
          "source": "CultureBotHT",
          "notes": "Imported from CultureBotHT. CAS-RN 7791-07-3 present, but no CHEBI entry exists (checked OAK CHEBI sqlite + PubChem CID synonyms). FEBA/Hans80 panels: Hans80metals, FEBA_stress. Used in 2 CultureBot media; samples: ALP defined perchlorate, ALP_defined_perchlorate. Curator can promote to a CHEBI primary if/when CHEBI adds the term."
        },
        {
          "evidence_type": "DATABASE_MATCH",
          "source": "CHEBI via OLS (stem-substring)",
          "notes": "Parent class identified via stem-substring; matched_via='Sodium perchlorate monohydrate'"
        },
        {
          "evidence_type": "DATABASE_MATCH",
          "source": "MIM curation (#342)",
          "notes": "mapping_quality NARROW_MATCH -> CLOSE_MATCH, predicate skos:narrowMatch -> skos:closeMatch. narrowMatch asserts this record is *narrower in meaning* than CHEBI:132103 ('sodium perchlorate') — a subsumption ChEBI itself denies: it files hydrates under CHEBI:35505 'hydrate', never under the anhydrous compound, which is not an ancestor even transitively. A hydrate is a distinct substance containing the anhydrous form, not a specialization of it. closeMatch claims similarity without subsumption. The ontology_id and the record's own identifier are unchanged."
        },
        {
          "evidence_type": "DATABASE_MATCH",
          "source": "MIM curation (#901); PubChem CID 516899; ChEBI:132103",
          "notes": "PubChem CID 516899 records CAS 7791-07-3 and formula ClH2NaO5; its water-containing InChI agrees with this monohydrate. CHEBI:132103 sodium perchlorate has the distinct water-free formula ClO4.Na and CAS 7601-89-0. Current MAPPING_SEMANTICS section 3 and its form-of ruling support the identity-retaining parent broadMatch and native B1 repair authorized by #901 comment 6565222455, not subclass projection or exact parent identity. The bounded searches did not resolve an exact eligible grounding. SNOMED 765356005 remains an unverified label-only lead: primary concept access was blocked and the native source enum lacks SNOMED. This does not establish global absence or disprove an exact term, and grants no registry workaround. Sigma71852 was not inspected because the request timed out. No role or release approval is implied. Archived sources: https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/516899 ; https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI:132103 ."
        }
      ]
    },
