      "All old pipe-separated source tokens survive. Added generator/manifest lineage is provenance, not independent chemical corroboration or source acceptance."
    ],
    "prior_row_reason": "The actual sodium perchlorate monohydrate row is supported as a form-of skos:broadMatch to CHEBI:132103 sodium perchlorate. Archived PubChem CID516899 has one water component in addition to the sodium/perchlorate structure represented by the water-free ChEBI parent. The parent row has empty other and validation_method cells, resolving the old hydrate-CAS alias leakage and providing an explicit asymmetric relation instead of inherited closeMatch approval. This supports the bounded relation, not global exhaustion of exact ontology alternatives.",
