          "notes": "Grounded to the ChEBI class CHEBI:16646 ('carbohydrate'): the label names a CATEGORY, and a ChEBI class is what a category should map to — the mirror image of #322, where records naming specific substances were wrongly on class terms. NARROW_MATCH because sugars are a proper subset of carbohydrates: ChEBI carries no `sugar` synonym on CHEBI:16646, so this is a real subclass relation and not a naming variant. Rule B1 then requires a sibling registry row, so the record takes a kgmicrobe.compound mint."
